From 06adf9e85c4d257f6f045b30d2c8f394f2e7bd1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Khansa Zahid <khansa@example.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 07:25:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Week 7: Use shared currency formatter wired to Settings, fix
 unused imports

- Added src/utils/currency.js (formatCurrency) and
  src/hooks/useCurrencySymbol.js, replacing 7 separate copy-pasted
  formatCurrency definitions across Dashboard, SaleList, SaleCreate,
  SaleInvoice, StockReport, SalesReport, and PurchasesReport.
- None of those duplicated copies actually used the currency_symbol
  application setting added in Week 6 (some had no symbol at all,
  ProductList hardcoded "$"); every price display now reads the
  configured symbol via useCurrencySymbol().
- Fixed a formatting glitch in StockReport.jsx where two <td> tags had
  been merged onto one line.
- Removed unused 'React' import (ESLint no-unused-vars) from
  PurchaseCreate.jsx and PurchaseList.jsx.
- Verified with npm run build (succeeds) and eslint (no new errors
  introduced by these changes).
